Do not recheck a definition inside an inline method when its info is asked for

The body of an inline method is not capture checked where it is defined,
only where it is expanded. But a definition inside it with an inferred type
has a completer which rechecks it, and that completer runs whenever the
symbol's info is asked for: by the final pass over the unit, say, which
walks inline bodies too, and takes a member as seen from a prefix. The
definition is then checked out of order, outside the environment of its
method, against types the method's own inline calls have not been expanded
to meet, and a closure which captures a context parameter was reported as
not conforming to the parameter type of an inline method.

Such a definition is now marked complete without being rechecked.

Found in Soundness's jacinta, in the inline `conjunction` of a derivation.

